<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6025" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caelĭcŏla</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coel-</span></b> ), ae (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen. plur.</i>
			caelicolūm, Enn. ap. <i><span class="en">Prisc. p.
			1103</span></i> P., or Ann. v 483 Vahl.; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 3,
				21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prud. Sym. 1, 170</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caelicolarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					13, 42</span></i>
			), adj.
			caelumcolo. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Dwelling in heaven</i>, <b>poet.</b> designation of <i>a deity</i>, <i>a god</i>, Enn. l. l.; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 2,
				641</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 554</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 787</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 1,
				174</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 637</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 5,
				111</span></i>; <i><span class="en">App. de Deo Socr.
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A worshipper of the heavens</i>, Cod. Th. 16, 5,
			43; 16, 8, 19; <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 1, 9</span></i>; cf.
				<i><span class="en">Juv.
				14, 97</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
